{
  "key": "gh-1956",
  "fields": {
    "summary": "[GOAL] reply auto-spill: oversized child replies spill to an artifact automatically — parent gets excerpt + agent:// ref + completeness, manual chunking retired to fallback",
    "description": "**[WIP][GOAL] reply auto-spill: an oversized child reply spills to an artifact automatically — the parent receives a bounded excerpt + `agent://` reference + completeness marker; the model never chunks manually**\n\n## Goal — delivery logistics belong to the harness (v1)\nOne sentence: **a child calls `reply` with whatever it has; if the message exceeds the spill threshold the harness stores the full text as an artifact and delivers excerpt + `agent://` pointer + completeness to the parent — manual chunking (`report_id`/`part_index`) becomes unnecessary, and the reply message budget stops being a model-side burden.**\nOwner rationale (2026-10-29): the child's output is nearly always far below the receiving side's input budget, so the per-message cap exists only as a distillation guardrail and transport bound — not because the parent cannot afford the text. When the text IS large, persistence-to-file + reference is the natural delivery: the parent reads the reference on demand.\n\n## Capability surface\n| Path | Contract |\n|---|---|\n| reply ≤ threshold | delivered verbatim as today (distillation guardrail intact) |\n| reply > threshold | harness auto-spills: full text → artifact store; parent gets bounded excerpt (~1–2k chars) + `agent://` pointer + completeness marker (`complete: true`, byte count) |\n| Parent follow-up | the pointer resolves via the existing `agent://<id>/<path>` addressing (read tool / task output addressing) — no new transport |\n| Child UX | the child's tool result says exactly what happened (`delivered via artifact (N bytes), ref agent://…`) — truthful ack per #1951 semantics |\n| Chunk protocol | stays for compatibility (existing consumers, mail fabric); auto-spill is the default path, manual chunking degrades to fallback |\n| Kill switch | config to restore pure-chunk behavior (default: auto-spill on) |\n\n## Acceptance criteria (testable)\n- **AC1** — UT: reply above threshold → artifact written (content byte-identical)